BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creating a Digital Archive in Collection Builder — Providence
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261118T120000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261118T133000
DTSTAMP:20261119T204145Z
UID:d9ce8c7aea0e6401c1e7a03133d5@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures\, Seminars and Workshops\,Providence\,
 United States
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning how to create lightweight\, sustainable
  digital archives? Collection Builder is an open-source framework for buil
 ding metadata-driven\, customizable digital archives. Collection Builder r
 elies on static site technology and the principles of minimal computing\, 
 and helps you learn fundamental skills like working with Github\, Markdown
 \, and HTML. In this workshop\, we will walk you through the steps of crea
 ting your own digital archive using demo metadata and items\, or bring you
 r own! Want to learn git and Github fundamentals before getting started? C
 heck out our prior workshop (suggested but not required.) This is a hybrid
  workshop that you can join in-person at the Rockefel\nCategory: Lectures
 \, Seminars and Workshops\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/libr
 ary/event/337137-creating-a-digital-archive-in-collection-builder
LOCATION:Rockefeller Library\, Rockefeller Library
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.brown.edu/library/event/337137-creating-a-digital-archi
 ve-in-collection-builder
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:brown-arts
END:VEVENT
