 ates
DESCRIPTION:Al Gore and Rep. Maxwell Frost discuss climate\, democracy\, a
 ffordability and their hopes for the future. Twenty years ago\, former Vic
 e President Al Gore and The Climate Reality Project set out to turn everyd
 ay citizens into leaders. Today\, we find ourselves posing the question: w
 ith a new Congress\, will there be fresh opportunities for progress? This 
 is an in-person event. No livestream will be available. Vice President Gor
 e\, who has spent decades pushing the climate crisis to the center of publ
 ic debate\, is joined by Congressman Maxwell Frost\, a longtime organizer 
 who brings the urgency of a new generation to Capitol Hill. Together\, the
 y’ll hold a cross-generational conversation on the road\nCategory: Lectu
 res & Speakers\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/the-impor
 tance-of-climate-leadership-and-the-power-of-public-action
