DESCRIPTION:This is a public-facing lecture and reception to accompany the
  exhibition "Unfossilizing African Art" on view now at the Brady Gallery. 
 Read more about the exhibition: Unfossilizing African Art - Presented afte
 r extensive research\, this exhibition recontextualizes African material c
 ulture objects held in the GW Collection for nearly 50 years. Led by Assis
 tant Professor Clement Akpang\, 59 students from four seminar courses offe
 red between Fall 2024 and Spring 2026\, conducted original research to dee
 pen understanding of the university’s holdings and update how we interpr
 et and exhibit these objects. The exhibition features 37 tangible heritage
  objects\, ranging from an Egúngún Paaka from Yoruba\nCategory: Arts & C
 ulture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/reimagining-the-c
 anon-african-art-display-and-interpretation
