SUMMARY:Eric Gottesman’s NIGHT AND DAY — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261204T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261204T170000
DTSTAMP:20261119T204145Z
UID:be63bdf31021fe1dbba255ab3cc0@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:For Freedoms presents artist and educator Eric Gottesman’s N
 IGHT AND DAY which centers on Ethiopian journalist and author Baalu Girma
 ’s controversial 1984 Amharic novel Oromay \, written under the Derg reg
 ime and banned shortly after its publication. Drawing on Gottesman’s dee
 p engagement with the novel\, NIGHT AND DAY considers how artists create\,
  communicate\, and sustain cultural memory within and against conditions o
 f censorship\, political repression\, and state violence. The exhibition e
 xtends beyond the gallery through a library of banned books\, a self-guide
 d workshop station that invites visitors to respond to censorship through 
 writing and drawing\, and a public conversation on how artist\nCategory: A
 rts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/eric-gotte
 smans-night-and-day
LOCATION:Flagg Building\, 500 17th Street NW\, Washington DC 20006
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/eric-gottesmans-night-and-day
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Food\, Flow\, Photography Gallery Presentation — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261204T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261204T150000
DTSTAMP:20261119T204145Z
UID:bcd0b48dfb63603938e43854f3ac@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Exhibition\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:All are invited to a photographic poster presentation where st
 udents in the Food\, Flow\, Photography course will showcase their final p
 rojects! This unique class\, supported by the Global Food Institute \, Mec
 hanical & Aerospace Engineering \, and Corcoran School of the Arts & Desig
 n \, brings science and art together. Students reveal the hidden physics o
 f fluid flows (gases and liquids) through the art of cooking. They experim
 ented with techniques to visualize flows in soups\, sauces\, mocktails\, c
 offee\, tea\, caramelization\, and more. It is science you can see and art
  you can feel. Mark your calendar and prepare to be amazed!\nCategory: Exh
 ibition\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/food-flow-photog
 raphy-gallery26
LOCATION:Science & Engineering Hall\, 800 22nd Street NW\, Washington DC 2
 0052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/food-flow-photography-gallery26
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
